  "title": "Gaza Displacement Camps Under Heavy Rain and Flooding, Eight Children Among 21 Killed, Israeli Demolition in Hebron",
  "summary": "Heavy rains and strong winds caused significant damage to Gaza's displacement camps, with tents collapsing and health ministry reports that five Palestinians were killed in a sand embankment collapse. Al Jazeera reports that the initial losses are estimated at about $3m. Eight children among 21 were killed in a war-damaged Gaza building collapse, with rescuers estimating that dozens of people are missing beneath the rubble of a building hit by an Israeli strike last year. Israeli forces begin demolishing Palestinian buildings in Hebron after two Israeli soldiers were killed in an attack by Palestinian gunmen at a checkpoint outside the West Bank city.",
